#
# Fan curves for the Arduino Ventuno Q.
#
# These only take effect for a profile that says FAN MODE curve. Under the default
# FAN MODE kernel the board's own thermal governor keeps the fan.
#
# Units are mandatory, as in profiles.conf. Points must ascend in temperature and
# must not step down as it gets hotter.
#
# The fan has 11 states, 0-10, where pwm = round(state * 255 / 10).
# MIN_STATE 2 is strongly advised: at state 1 the tachometer misreads, so fan speed cannot be trusted there.
# State 0 (off) stays available regardless.
#
# What this zone does ON THE BOARD'S OWN HEATSINK AND FAN, open, with no enclosure around
# it, measured here with all 8 cores loaded:
#   idle, fan off              36-37C
#   full load, fan off         47C after two minutes, and still creeping
#   full load, fan state 4     41C
#   full load, fan state 10    41C - on THIS cooler, past state 4 buys nothing measurable
#   full load, intake blocked  about 5C above whatever it holds clear
#
# Two different things follow, and only the first is about your hardware:
#   - In the measured band the useful detail is between 38C and 47C, so that is where the
#     shipped curves put their points. Above ~41C on this cooler the zone is reporting
#     airflow that is not delivering rather than load.
#   - Above the measured band the points are HEADROOM, not decoration. A different
#     heatsink, a slower or faster fan, an enclosure, or extra case fans all move the
#     envelope up, and none of that can be measured from here. Keep a path to the top
#     state in every curve: the only thing above a curve is the 85C clamp, which is a
#     hard stop and not a cooling policy.

# ==========
# FAN CURVES
# ==========
< CURVE NAME=desktop >
  ZONE cpuss-0-0
  POINT 30C STATE 0       # off below 30C
  POINT 38C STATE 4       # 40%, where the stock config jumps to; holds 41C under load
  POINT 43C STATE 6       # above anything load alone produces here: airflow is down
  POINT 45C STATE 8       # measured with the intake blocked
  POINT 47C STATE 10      # 100%; the measured ceiling with no fan at all
  HYSTERESIS 4C
  MIN_STATE 2
  POLL 2s
  FAILSAFE kernel
>

# Quieter: starts later, tops out lower, and a wide hysteresis so it changes speed rarely.
# Used by the 'quiet' profile, whose raised 45C trip is what the kernel does with the fan
# if this curve's FAILSAFE hands the zone back.
< CURVE NAME=quiet >
  ZONE cpuss-0-0
  POINT 30C STATE 0
  POINT 44C STATE 2       # load alone holds 41C at state 4, so nothing below this
  POINT 46C STATE 4
  POINT 48C STATE 6       # the top of what the OE cooler reaches
  POINT 55C STATE 8       # headroom: unreachable here, but another heatsink or an
  POINT 65C STATE 10      # enclosure moves the whole envelope up
  HYSTERESIS 8C
  MIN_STATE 2
  POLL 5s
  FAILSAFE kernel
>

# For sustained load: on early, climbs fast, and FAILSAFE full so that losing the
# daemon leaves the fan at maximum rather than handing a hot board back to a
# governor whose only active trip is at 38C.
< CURVE NAME=sustained >
  ZONE cpuss-0-0
  POINT 30C STATE 3       # on at idle, before the load arrives
  POINT 38C STATE 6
  POINT 42C STATE 8
  POINT 45C STATE 10
  HYSTERESIS 3C
  MIN_STATE 2
  POLL 1s
  FAILSAFE full
>

< CURVE NAME=fallback >
  ZONE cpuss-0-0
  POINT 30C STATE 0       # off below 30C
  POINT 40C STATE 6
  POINT 50C STATE 10
  HYSTERESIS 3C
  MIN_STATE 2
  POLL 1s
  FAILSAFE full
>

# ==================
# TARGET TEMPERATURE
# ==================
# TARGET blocks are a different KIND, not a curve with a flag. A CURVE is a stateless
# lookup; a TARGET is a closed-loop controller that needs history and a clock.
# Used by the 'held40' profile. 40C is at the edge of this board's reach: no fan state
# holds a loaded board below 40.9C, so DEADBAND 1C had the controller stepping to maximum
# for the last 0.2C - measured, 2 -> 7 in 90s with the temperature flat at 41.2C.
< TARGET NAME=held40 >
  ZONE cpuss-0-0
  TARGET 40C
  DEADBAND 2C             # satisfied 38-42C, which is where a loaded board sits
  MIN_STATE 2
  STEP_INTERVAL 15s     # the board's thermal time constant, not the poll rate
  POLL 2s
  FAILSAFE kernel
>

# ==========
# FAN HEALTH
# ==========
# Fan (airflow) health. ONE block per file.
#
# The delta is signed and BOTH directions mean something, assume:
#   above baseline -> restricted intake, blocked airflow
#   below baseline -> the fan is not delivering: bearing wear, dust-loaded impeller, etc.
#
# This needs a reference first, captured on YOUR board, if applicable in YOUR enclosure:
#   sudo qcctl --fan-baseline capture
#
# If You comment this block out and nothing is judged.
< AIRFLOW >
  DELTA    8%
  DEBOUNCE 3
>
